#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# tanh

#% text
# `tanh(x)` gives the hyperbolic tangent `sinh(x)/cosh(x)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `tanh(0)` is 0 and `tanh(-x)` is `-tanh(x)`; the value tends to 1 as `x` tends to `inf`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values, without overflow for large arguments. `tanh` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
tanh(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
tanh(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.7615941559557649

#% cell
tanh(1000.0)
#% output
#= 1.0

#% cell
n(tanh(1), 30)
#% output
#= 0.7615941559557648881194582826047936

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(tanh(x), x)
#% output
#= cosh(x)^-2

#% text
# The relation to the logistic function:

#% cell
tanh(0.6) - (2*logistic_sigmoid(1.2) - 1)
#% output
#= 2.220446049250313e-16

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sinh`, `cosh`, `tan`, `logistic_sigmoid`
